NAME
       nc - read and write network connections

SYNOPSIS
       nc [-u] [host] <port>
       nc [-u] -l <port>

DESCRIPTION
       Connects to a port, or listens on one, and shuttles data between
       the socket and the terminal.

OPTIONS
       -u     use UDP instead of TCP
       -l     listen rather than connect

EXAMPLES
       nc -l 9000
       nc 10.0.0.1 9000

SEE ALSO
       nmap(1), httpd(1), ssh(1)
